1	// The work ledger: the controller's signed record of who is working on what, at which stage, with which inputs
2	// and outputs. The status ledger (packages/ledger/status.mjs) stays authoritative for an item's status and only
3	// the owner signs it; this ledger records the governed lifecycle that produces the evidence a status proposal
4	// cites. Every receiving stage re-derives its handoff from this ledger before it proceeds.
5	//
6	// Kinds (schema ophanim.work/v1), each re-derived on append and on every verify:
7	//   work.intake   a source of work seen by reconciliation: a status item, a published issue, a ticket. An issue
8	//                 with no ledger item is a CANDIDATE: it is recorded, never executed, until the owner adds an item.
9	//   work.claim    the controller takes one stage of one item: attempt, idempotency key, lease, budget. Refused
10	//                 while another unreleased, unexpired claim on the same item exists (no duplicate execution), and
11	//                 refused when the same idempotency key already completed (no paying twice for the same inputs).
12	//                 A FENCED claim (payload `fence: 1`, every claim this module writes) is also refused while ANY earlier
13	//                 claim on the item is unreleased, expired or not: `claim()` first releases an expired one as `expired`,
14	//                 so two claims can never both lead to recorded stages (independent review, assignment 3, Q3/Q4).
15	//   work.release  the claim ends: completed, returned, failed, blocked, interrupted or expired. Cites its claim.
16	//   work.spend    provider calls CHARGED under a claim, recorded (signed) BEFORE the calls are made: {item, stage,
17	//                 attempt, provider_calls (cumulative for the claim), at}. A call that already left the process is
