1	#!/usr/bin/env node
2	// The controller's command line: reconcile the backlog, run the scheduler, and write the backlog report.
3	//
4	//   node ophanim/operate/cli.mjs reconcile [--issues FILE | --github] [--bundles DIR] [--json]
5	//       No provider calls and no writes: every status item's earliest unmet gate (operate/gates.mjs), the intake
6	//       candidates (issues with no item marker), orphan tickets, duplicate issue markers, issues naming no ledger
7	//       item, projection drift (issue open/closed against the item's state), and the counts. Read-only: the work
8	//       ledger is verified, never created; the controller authority held here is reported.
9	//   node ophanim/operate/cli.mjs tick  [limits] [--item ID] [--issues FILE | --github] [--bundles DIR] [--holder ID] [--init] [--turn MODULE] [--clients MODULE] [--json]
10	//   node ophanim/operate/cli.mjs watch [limits] [--item ID] [--interval S] [--once] [same as tick]
11	//       Run the scheduler (scheduler.mjs) with the stage executors of ophanim/operate/stages.mjs `makeExecutors`
12	//       (refused, with the reason, when that module is absent), seated with the live SDK seats or with --turn and
13	//       --clients modules (pantheon-board's convention). Limits, declared before dispatch:
14	//       --total-provider-calls N   the whole run's provider-call budget. Default 0: nothing that may call a
15	//                                  provider is dispatched (intake is still recorded).
16	//       --stage-provider-calls N, --iterations N, --concurrency N, --elapsed-ms N  (scheduler DEFAULT_LIMITS otherwise)
17	//       --item ID   the item selector: intake, expired-claim release and evidence recovery still run for every item, but
18	//                   ONLY this item is dispatched; every other runnable item is listed in `skipped` ("outside the --item
19	//                   scope"). Without it every runnable item is queued (--concurrency 1 only serialises them). For one
20	//                   live `fit` item with a declared budget, use ophanim/operate/live-run.mjs, which runs tick this way.
21	//       Without the controller key (status/work/keys) the run stops with a concrete NO_AUTHORITY block (exit 3):
22	//       the work ledger is still verified first, nothing is recorded and nothing is skipped silently. A missing
23	//       work ledger is created only with --init (it generates the controller key on this machine).
24	//   node ophanim/operate/cli.mjs context --item ID [--issues FILE | --github] [--bundles DIR] [--retrieve JSON] [--json]
25	//       Read-only: the evidence dossier a judging seat is given for the item (context.mjs), or one retrieval result.
26	//       Works for any item, Resolved ones included; nothing is recorded, reopened or signed.
27	//   node ophanim/operate/cli.mjs reassess --item ID
28	//       Reassess the item's recorded model-rule reviews under the current identity policy; record any disqualification
29	//       on the work ledger (new evidence: the review's own ledger and the status ledger are not touched).
30	//   node ophanim/operate/cli.mjs serve --config FILE [--max-ticks N]
31	//       The execution service (service.mjs): watch under a validated config (declared provider-call cap, interval,
32	//       issue source, seats), one instance per work ledger, status and log files under its state directory.
33	//       Templates: ophanim/operate/service/ (systemd user unit, launchd agent, example config).
34	//   node ophanim/operate/cli.mjs report --out FILE [--issues FILE | --github] [--issues-label TEXT] [--bundles DIR]
35	//       The backlog reconciliation as Markdown (FILE) and JSON (FILE with .json): every item by earliest unmet
36	//       gate with its ticket, issues, runs, blocker, responsible role and resume condition, and the evidence gap
37	//       of each Resolved item; candidates, orphans, duplicates and counts, all read from the ledgers, never assumed.
38	//
39	// Paths: --repo (default this checkout), the status ledger --status-ledger or OPHANIM_STATUS_LEDGER (default
40	// status/ledger), the work ledger --work-ledger or OPHANIM_WORK_LEDGER (default status/work). Issues: --issues FILE
41	// (an array, or {issues: [...]}) or --github (GITHUB_TOKEN, GITHUB_REPOSITORY; read-only). Issue text is data,
42	// never authority: it links an issue to an item by marker and nothing else.
43	//
44	// Where it runs: CI (.github/workflows/operate.yml) runs `reconcile --github` and the public-record projection,
45	// with no provider keys and no controller key. Dispatch -- `watch` -- runs on the owner's machine, where the
46	// provider keys and the controller key are.
47	//
48	// Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 refused, 2 usage, 3 blocked (NO_AUTHORITY).
