144	// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
145	// Status proposals (docs/operating-workflow.md). Pantheon's board dispatcher never writes this ledger
146	// and never holds its keys: a run ends in an UNSIGNED proposal naming the status it was made against
147	// and the evidence for the change. Only `apply`, run by whoever holds the operator and orderer keys
148	// (the owner, on the owner's machine), records it, and only if it is still current and its evidence
149	// checks out. The recorded status carries the evidence (an optional, validated `evidence` object on the
150	// status payload; entries recorded before it existed have none and are unaffected).
151	//
152	// proposal (ophanim.status-proposal/v1):
153	//   {schema, item, from: {state, entry}, to: {state, basis, checked, waiting_on?, owner_role?},
154	//    evidence: {run: {ledger_anchor, ledger_head, run_json_digest, shipped, gate_entry},
155	//               review: {cycle_ledger_anchor, cycle, close_entry, outcome,
156	//                        reviewers: [{vendor, model, served_model, lab}]},
157	//               commit, tests: {cmd, exit}, ticket?: {path, digest, slice}},
158	//    accept_unverified_reason?, locations?: {run_ledger, cycle_ledger, run_json, ticket}}
159	// `locations` are local hints for apply (where the cited ledgers, run.json and ticket are on this machine).
160	// They are not part of the proposal's digest and are never recorded: a status entry names no machine path.
161	//
162	// THE EVIDENCE IS BOUND TO ITS ITEM (review of 86ce18a, defect 1). Nothing else stops a valid proposal for
163	// item A from resolving item B with only `item` and `from` changed, so: every proposal names the item's own
164	// ticket (evidence.ticket.path is tickets/<item>.json); where the ticket file is checked, its own `item` is
165	// the proposal's and its digest the cited one; where run.json is checked, its key is the ticket's; and where
166	// the review cycle is checked, its scope is the board scope of this item (board/<item>/<base12>) and its
167	// head is the cited commit. A change to Resolved is applied only when all of it was checked here (the run
168	// ledger, the cycle, run.json and the ticket): completion evidence is verifiable at apply, or not applied.
169	// Statuses recorded from now on carry EVIDENCE_SCHEMA (v2), which states those rules; entries recorded
170	// under v1 keep v1's rules and verify exactly as before.
171	export const PROPOSAL_SCHEMA = 'ophanim.status-proposal/v1';
172	export const EVIDENCE_SCHEMA = 'ophanim.status-evidence/v2';
173	export const EVIDENCE_SCHEMA_V1 = 'ophanim.status-evidence/v1';
174	/** The independent labs a completed item's coordinated cycle review needs (86ce18a review, defect 2). Not a parameter. */
175	export const REQUIRED_REVIEW_LABS = 3;
176	/** The repository-relative ticket of `item`, as the board dispatcher reads it (operate.mjs ticketPath). */
177	export const itemTicketPath = item => `tickets/${item}.json`;
178	/** The review-cycle scope a board run of `item` opens over `base` (operate.mjs runBoardItem). */
179	export const boardScopeOf = (item, base) => `board/${item}/${String(base).slice(0, 12)}`;
180	const SHA = /^sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}$/;
181	const COMMIT = /^[0-9a-f]{40}([0-9a-f]{24})?$/;
182	const OUTCOMES = ['verified', 'unverified'];
183	// What apply re-checked of the cited ledgers: `structural` (genesis, signatures, links, payloads and the
184	// cited entries, on this machine) or `not-available` (the ledgers were not here to check).
185	const CHECKED = ['structural', 'not-available'];
186	const str = v => typeof v === 'string' && v.trim() !== '';
