1	// The operating loop over the status board (docs/operating-workflow.md).
2	//
3	// Pantheon reads the AUTHORITATIVE board (the status ledger, packages/ledger/status.mjs, which must
4	// verify), takes the items that are dispatchable, seats a team for one, runs it through its real
5	// pipeline (runOpenItem: plan, work, acceptance, in-run review, ship), commits the shipped change on a
6	// branch, has the change reviewed by independent reviewers on distinct labs (reviewCycle, every turn and
7	// review on the run's ledger), and ends in an evidence bundle and an UNSIGNED status proposal.
8	//
9	// It never writes the status ledger and never needs its keys. Recording the proposal is `status.mjs
10	// apply`, run by the key holder (the owner, on the owner's machine).
11	//
12	// An item is dispatchable iff its latest status is Ready, every item it depends on is Resolved, and a
13	// valid ticket exists for it at tickets/<item>.json that has not already been applied (the latest status
14	// entry's evidence names a different ticket digest, or none). A ticket names one bounded slice of the
15	// item's work, honestly: a slice that leaves the rest of the item to do proposes Ready again, with the
16	// slice recorded; only a ticket that covers the whole item proposes Resolved.
17	//
18	// Every vendor SDK stays at the edge: `makeClientFor` (the seats) and `turn` (the cycle reviewers) are
19	// injected, as for runOpenItem and reviewCycle.
