2	// pantheon/src/route/fit-matrix.mjs). Complete lifecycle runs with NO profile named: the scheduler, the stage
3	// executors, Pantheon's FIVE-STAGE SPECIALIST PIPELINE (pantheon/src/pipeline) and the ledgers, end to end.
4	//
5	//   Stage 1  the plan stage's planner writes `work_units` with the plan (three labs review them with it)
6	//   Stage 2  an OpenAI dispatcher per unit, by the unit's difficulty          (scripted single-turn seat)
7	//   Stage 3  an Antigravity lane per unit, in the unit's own worktree         (the fixture's fake agy CLI: a real
8	//                                                                               child process that writes files)
9	//   Stage 4  a Grok subagent over the unit's A2A shim                          (scripted single-turn seat)
10	//   Stage 5  the dispatcher's exact model, pinned                              (scripted single-turn seat)
11	//   then     the coordinated three-lab change review, the validator and the outcome, unchanged.
12	//
13	// Every provider is scripted or the fake CLI: these show routing, scheduling, escalation and recording, not model
14	// judgment and not a live quota.
