1	// THE FIT ROUTING MATRIX (owner direction 2026-11-17). One table: role x difficulty -> the seat `fit` starts on.
2	// Pure data and pure functions; nothing here calls a provider or reads a ticket.
3	//
4	//   role         easy                       medium                    hard
5	//   planner      Anthropic's sonnet         opus (newest declared)    the top Anthropic seat   (ids: FIT_MATRIX below)
6	//   dispatcher   gpt-6-luna                 gpt-6.1-sol               gpt-6-astra
7	//   implementer  gemini-4-hydrogen-medium   gemini-4-hydrogen-high    gemini-4-carbon-high     (Antigravity lanes)
8	//   subagent     grok-4.6                   grok-4.6                  grok-4.7
9	//   reviewer     the EXACT model the dispatcher of that unit ran on (pinned); it escalates only inside OpenAI
10	//
11	// The medium dispatcher is gpt-6.1-sol (owner correction, same day); every other OpenAI medium seat stays gpt-6-sol.
12	//
13	// GEMINI GOES THROUGH ANTIGRAVITY FIRST. An implementer seat is an Antigravity lane (lanes.json, transport agy-cli);
14	// its failover ladder is more lanes, in the order below. The metered Gemini API id of a lane's base model is never a
15	// rung: it is the QUOTA failover of that lane, used only when the lane attempt is refused for quota (HTTP 429 / quota
16	// exhausted, as packages/model-client classifyFailure classifies it). Any other lane failure does not reach it.
17	//
18	// A REJECTION raises the lane's thinking level first (same base model, the next level `agy models` offers), and only
19	// then steps to the next rung of the ladder: hydrogen-medium -> hydrogen-high -> hydrogen-xhigh -> next rung;
20	// carbon-high has no level above it -> next rung.
21	//
22	// The difficulty is the ticket's label RAISED by the task profile's floors (stakes; ambiguity for the planner): a
23	// floor can move a pick up a column, never down (frontier.mjs fitLevel).
24	import { MODELS, LANES, modelId } from "../config/models.mjs";
