1	// Review every cycle, on the ledger (docs/cycle-review.md items 2 and 5-6; docs/STATUS.md
2	// `review-every-cycle`). A cycle checked only by its author shipped a regression; the layered review
3	// found it. So the review is not a pass someone remembers to run: it is a chain of entries, and a cycle
4	// does not close until they re-derive.
5	//
6	//   cycle               {scope, base, head, diff_sha, files, prompt_sha, brief_sha, reviewers, author_labs,
7	//                        opened_at}. The change under review: two commit ids of the repository and the
8	//                       digest of the diff between them. Opened by the controller. Cycles of one scope
9	//                       form a contiguous chain: a cycle's base is the previous cycle's head, and it cites
10	//                       that cycle's close, so no range of commits goes unreviewed and no cycle opens
11	//                       while the previous one is still open. It may cite the author's turns.
12	//   review (lineage)    each reviewer's verdict, signed by the reviewing seat and citing the cycle (and so,
13	//                       through it, the author turns): cold review applies (lineage-kinds.mjs). It names
14	//                       the turn that answered, which must have been given exactly the cycle's prompt.
15	//                       One review per lab per cycle, and never the lab that authored the change.
16	//   finding             {review, index, severity, file, line, claim, reproduction}: one structured
17	//                       finding, re-derived from the reviewer's signed reply (it must be finding `index`
18	//                       of that reply, as parseReview reads it), so the controller can neither invent
19	//                       nor reword one. `reproduction` is a command or test, or null when the reviewer
20	//                       gave none.
21	//   finding.resolution  {status: fixed, fix: {commit, test, before: {commit, exit}, after: {commit, exit}}}
22	//                       or {status: deferred, reason}. A fix names a later commit and a test that exited
23	//                       non-zero on the reviewed head and zero on the fix.
24	//   cycle.close         {outcome, reviews, labs, findings: {total, fixed, deferred, unreproduced}}: the
25	//                       close is a CLAIM the ledger re-derives from the cycle's entries. It holds only if
26	//                       every review is recorded on distinct labs, every finding a reviewer reported is
27	//                       recorded, and every finding is fixed or deferred. The outcome is not chosen:
28	//                       `verified` when every finding carries a reproduction, `unverified` otherwise.
29	//
30	//   cycle.attempt       {seat: {vendor, model, lab}, attempt, max_attempts, outcome, why, resumed, at}: one
31	//                       reviewer seat's try at the cycle (independent review 2026-11-16, C2). A failed try
32	//                       (a 503, a refused review) is recorded with its reason, and the cycle can be RESUMED:
33	//                       only the seats that have no review are tried again, under the same prompt, and the
34	//                       reviews already recorded stand. Attempts of one lab are numbered 1, 2, ... and never
35	//                       pass the cycle's max_attempts (the same on every attempt of the cycle); a lab whose
36	//                       attempt was `reviewed` is not tried again. Additive: a cycle opened before this kind
37	//                       existed has no attempts, and its close re-derives exactly as before.
38	//
39	//   practice.disposition  (practice-kinds.mjs; independent review 2026-11-16, C3) the cycle's practice
40	//                       assessment and any candidate's disposition. The CONTRACT a cycle opened under is on
41	//                       the cycle: `contract: pantheon.cycle/v2` (the default for a new cycle) also names the
42	//                       selection policy in effect {version, hash, profile}, the practice scope, and `prior`,
43	//                       the admitted practice decision it loaded at open (cited; null for none). Such a cycle
44	//                       closes only with at least one assessment-stage disposition, and its close lists them
45	//                       (`practice`). A cycle with no `contract` field opened under the old contract: it
46	//                       re-derives, closes and hashes exactly as before. A scope does not return from v2 to
47	//                       the old contract.
48	//
49	//   required_reviewers  (optional on a cycle; 86ce18a review, defect 2) the independent labs the cycle's review
50	//                       requires, recorded when it opens (board runs and the review-cycle CLI: REQUIRED_REVIEW_LABS,
51	//                       3). Such a cycle names at least that many reviewers, never fewer than REQUIRED_REVIEW_LABS,
52	//                       and closes (verified or not) only on that many distinct labs. A cycle without the field
53	//                       (every v1 and v2 cycle opened before it existed) validates, closes and hashes exactly as before.
54	//
55	// What re-derivation does NOT do: run the tests or the reproductions, or check that the fix commit is a
56	// descendant of the head. The fail-before / pass-after exits are recorded data (signed by the
57	// controller, like the gate's lease rows were), checked for presence and consistency only.
