68	//   every contract   three distinct labs on a qualifying panel: one review per lab per cycle, and required_reviewers.
69	//   v1, v2           no reviewer from a LAB that authored the change (`author_labs`). Unchanged: a cycle opened
70	//                    under v1 or v2 re-derives, closes and hashes exactly as before, now and always.
71	//   v3               no reviewer that IS a contributing MODEL (`author_models`, by identity: review/identity.mjs, so an
72	//                    effort level, alias, snapshot, session or route does not make a contributor eligible), and none
73	//                    from `excluded_labs` (labs of contributions that name a lab and no model). A reviewer from a lab
74	//                    that contributed is allowed, and the close records it (`shared_labs`).
75	//   v3 IDENTITY      a v3 cycle carries `identity_policy: {digest, rules}`: the WHOLE policy that resolves a model
76	//                    name to its identity and lab (review/identity.mjs), and `contributors`, the raw names it was
77	//                    opened with. Every check of the cycle -- who may review, which lab a review counts for, the
78	//                    seat's lab, the close -- uses those recorded rules, never the current configuration, so a later
79	//                    alias correction cannot change this cycle's validity. A reviewer whose asked-for or answering
80	//                    model the policy cannot resolve, or whose two names are of different labs, does not qualify.
81	/** Why a reviewer seat may not review cycle `c`, or null. `seat` is {vendor, model, served_model?, lab}. */
82	export function independenceRefusal(c, seat, {answer = false} = {}) {
83	  if (c.contract !== CYCLE_CONTRACT_V3) return c.author_labs.includes(seat.lab) ? `the ${seat.lab} lab authored the change and may not review it` : null;
